@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About </PageTitle>

<div class="about-page">
    <header class="page-header">
        <div>
            <h1>About This Site</h1>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="about-content">
        <h2>Why This Exists</h2>
        <p>
            I created this website to document recipes and meals that I like making.
            Rather than following recipes exactly, I often create variations based on what's available and what I'm craving.
            This catalog helps me remember what I've made so I can recreate favorites in the future.

            I also wanted to go back to coding with less AI, since I use AI at work extensively.
            So I figured I'd combine the two. Once I have enough recipes with aesthetic photos, 
            I'll probably print out a cookbook for myself and my family.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="system-design">
        <h2>System Design</h2>
        <p>
            Coming soon...
        </p>
        <!-- <p>
            This is a lightweight, free-to-deploy Blazor WebAssembly application built for simplicity and scalability.
            All data is stored as static JSON, and images are served from the wwwroot folder—no backend database required.
        </p> -->
    </section>
</div>

<style>
.about-page {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
}

.about-content, .system-design {
    margin: 2rem 0;
}
</style>
